SECTION 2 — BLOCKED. MUST NOT BE INTEGRATED INTO THE DISTRIBUTED CLIENT.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

These are incompatible with closed-source commercial distribution, with Apple
App Store distribution, or both. This list exists so that the decision is not
relitigated in a pull request.

  GPL / AGPL family -- linking (static OR dynamic) would require releasing the
  entire application under the same terms:

    MuPDF .......... AGPL-3.0 or commercial   PDF rendering
                     A paid commercial licence from Artifex is a legitimate
                     option if the business chooses to purchase one. Until then:
                     BLOCKED.
    Poppler ........ GPL-2.0-or-later         PDF rendering
    Xpdf ........... GPL or commercial        PDF rendering
    antiword ....... GPL                      Legacy .doc
    catdoc ......... GPL                      Legacy .doc
    wv ............. GPL                      Legacy .doc
    unrtf .......... GPL                      RTF
    DjVuLibre ...... GPL-2.0                  DjVu
    Xapian ......... GPL-2.0-or-later         Search
    x265 ........... GPL-2.0 or commercial    HEVC encoding

  LGPL-3.0 -- HARD BLOCK FOR THE iOS CLIENT.
  LGPL-3.0 inherits GPLv3's anti-tivoization / "Installation Information" terms.
  Apple's code signing means a user cannot install a relinked binary on a
  non-jailbroken device, so the relinking right cannot be exercised. The
  obligation therefore cannot be satisfied.

    libheif ........ LGPL-3.0                 HEIF container
    libde265 ....... LGPL-3.0                 HEVC decoding
    libmobi ........ LGPL-3.0                 MOBI e-books

  LGPL-2.1 -- AVOID. Static linking requires distributing relinkable object
  files, which obliges us to publish enough of our build for a third party to
  relink. Permissible in principle, unacceptable in practice here, and in every
  case below a permissive alternative exists.

    PoDoFo ......... LGPL-2.0+   (QPDF is the permissive alternative)
    ZBar ........... LGPL-2.1    (ZXing-C++ is the permissive alternative)
    librsvg ........ LGPL-2.1    (NanoSVG / resvg are the alternatives)
    LibRaw ......... LGPL-2.1 / CDDL   (camera RAW is out of scope)

  Proprietary / restrictive:

    unRAR .......... The licence forbids using the source to develop a
                     RAR-compatible archiver. Not OSI-approved. No permissive
                     alternative exists. RAR IS PERMANENTLY OUT OF SCOPE.

  Server-side licence notes (not client dependencies):

    Redis >= 7.4 ... RSALv2 / SSPL. Use Valkey (BSD-3-Clause) or Redis <= 7.2.4.
    Qt ............. GPL / LGPLv3 or commercial. A commercial licence is required
                     for closed static linking. Compose Multiplatform (Apache-2.0)
                     is preferred for desktop.

