SECTION 3 — CONDITIONAL, WITH STATED CONDITIONS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  LibreOffice .................... MPL-2.0 (with LGPLv3 components)
      ALLOWED: server-side only, invoked as a SEPARATE PROCESS
               (`soffice --headless --convert-to`). Invoking a separate program
               over a command line is aggregation, not linking, so MPL-2.0
               imposes no obligation on our own program.
      FORBIDDEN: embedding or linking into any client application.
      CONSEQUENCE: legacy binary DOC / XLS / PPT support is SERVER-ONLY and
               therefore NOT AVAILABLE OFFLINE. Gated on open question PQ-4.

  resvg .......................... MPL-2.0 (Rust)
      ALLOWED, with two conditions: (a) any modifications we make to
      MPL-covered FILES must be published; (b) it introduces a Rust toolchain
      into the mobile build. Decision deferred -- see docs/file-format-support.md
      section 7.5. NanoSVG (zlib) is the zero-new-toolchain alternative.

  FFmpeg ......................... LGPL-2.1+ (GPL if --enable-gpl)
      DEFERRED. Three independent problems: (1) LGPL static linking friction on
      iOS; (2) enabling x264/x265 flips the build to GPL; (3) H.264 / HEVC / AAC
      carry codec patent exposure independent of the software licence.
      DECISION: v1.0 ships NO transcoding. Playback and thumbnails use the
      platform media stack, where the OS vendor holds the codec licences. If
      transcoding becomes required (PQ-5), it is done SERVER-SIDE.

  HEIC / HEIF .................... BLOCKED on two independent grounds
      (1) Licence: the libheif stack is LGPL-3.0 / GPL-2.0 (Section 2).
      (2) Patents: HEVC is covered by active patent pools. Distributing an HEVC
          decoder may require a patent licence depending on jurisdiction and
          volume, independently of the software licence.
      DECISION: use the PLATFORM decoder on iOS and Android only, where the OS
      vendor has already licensed it. HEIC is NOT SUPPORTED on desktop or web.
      No HEIC encoding on any platform. AVIF (AV1, royalty-free via AOMedia) is
      the strategic alternative.

  Machine-learning model weights .. VARIOUS -- treated as dependencies
      Model weights carry licences that are NOT the runtime's licence.
        - Apache-2.0 / MIT weights ........ PREFERRED, default choice
        - "Community"/"open weights" with use restrictions (MAU thresholds,
          acceptable-use clauses, naming requirements) .. legal review required
          per version; conditions recorded here
        - Non-commercial (CC-BY-NC, research-only) ...... BLOCKED, never shipped
      Every shipped model gets an entry in this file with its exact version and
      licence, and is signature-verified before load.

